flags="HasNoZOC","IgZOC","NonMil","Provoking","Diplomat","Spy"
roles="DiplomatStartUnit"
helptext="A Spy is more skilled in the arts of espionage than her Diplomat predecessor.","She can perform all the functions of the Diplomat; refer to the Diplomat entry for more details. Unlike a Diplomat, a Spy may also survive an operation in a foreign city and become more experienced as a result. Spies are also more effective than Diplomats at defending cities against foreign Diplomats and Spies.","A Spy can also be used to:\n - sabotage an enemy unit (reducing its hit points to half), if it is alone on a tile and the players are at war;\n - poison the water supply of an enemy city (reducing the population by one);\n - steal specific technology (with a reduced chance of success);\n - steal further technologies from a city which has already been stolen from (although cities become more resistant each time they are stolen from);\n - sabotage predetermined city targets (with a reduced chance of success).","A Spy that survives the more aggressive actions (sabotage, theft, inciting rebellion, and poisoning) escapes to the safety of the nearest friendly city.","Spies built under a Communist government will start at the first veteran level (handler)."

[unit_46]
